.vercel
.env*
node_modules/
# The live database is NOT in the repository.
#
# local-data/db.json holds the real records: officer names, 10-digit mobile
# numbers, uploaded scan documents, item photographs, audit trails and live
# session tokens. Those must not be published, so the file is ignored and
# untracked. It is still version-controlled in the sense that matters day to
# day: the rotating copies under local-data/backups/ are the real safety net,
# and a change to the data still shows up as a change on this machine.
#
# What IS committed is local-data/db.demo.json - the same document with every
# person, number, token, photograph and audit entry replaced or removed. On the
# first run, when db.json does not exist, the app stands itself up from that
# copy, so a fresh clone opens on a working demo rather than an empty screen.
local-data/db.json
# An old pre-import copy of the database that used to be tracked. It carried 8
# accounts, a live session token and an un-hashed-era password hash, none of
# which belongs in a shared repository. The file stays on this machine.
local-data/db.before-import.json

# Local safety copies and the old Neon production dumps are never committed.
local-data/db.backup-*.json
# Whole-database copies taken before a password change. These are the size of
# the live database (hundreds of MB) and they hold the OLD password hashes, so
# they must never reach git - the backups/ pattern below does not match them
# because they sit directly in local-data/.
local-data/db-BEFORE-*.json
local-data/backups/
local-data/prod-*.json
local-data/prod-backups/
hp-inventory-image.tar
*.bak_*
*.bak
ims-server.log
vercel-deploy*.log
*.tmp

# Server stdout/stderr written by the local runner. Machine-local noise.
server-out.log
server-err.log

# One-off audit reports generated while checking a district or circle.
*-audit.html
